# Flink Event-Time Sessionization

## Goal
Detect sessions ("stages") for keyed event streams where a session ends after a fixed inactivity gap.

## Setup notes
- Use event time and watermarks; do not rely on processing time.
- If timestamps are in microseconds, convert to milliseconds for Flink event time APIs.

## Pattern A: KeyedProcessFunction + event-time timers
Use when you need custom state and output on inactivity.

```java
class StageCounter extends KeyedProcessFunction<Long, TaskEvent, Tuple2<Long, Integer>> {
  private final long gapMs = 10 * 60 * 1000L;
  private transient ValueState<Long> lastEventTs;
  private transient ValueState<Integer> currentCount;
  private transient ValueState<Integer> maxCount;

  @Override
  public void open(Configuration parameters) {
    lastEventTs = getRuntimeContext().getState(new ValueStateDescriptor<>("lastTs", Long.class));
    currentCount = getRuntimeContext().getState(new ValueStateDescriptor<>("curCnt", Integer.class));
    maxCount = getRuntimeContext().getState(new ValueStateDescriptor<>("maxCnt", Integer.class));
  }

  @Override
  public void processElement(TaskEvent e, Context ctx, Collector<Tuple2<Long, Integer>> out) throws Exception {
    long ts = e.eventTimeMs;
    Integer cur = currentCount.value();
    if (cur == null) cur = 0;
    cur++;
    currentCount.update(cur);

    Long last = lastEventTs.value();
    if (last != null) {
      // cancel previous timer if any
      ctx.timerService().deleteEventTimeTimer(last + gapMs);
    }
    lastEventTs.update(ts);
    ctx.timerService().registerEventTimeTimer(ts + gapMs);
  }

  @Override
  public void onTimer(long timestamp, OnTimerContext ctx, Collector<Tuple2<Long, Integer>> out) throws Exception {
    Integer cur = currentCount.value();
    if (cur == null) cur = 0;
    Integer max = maxCount.value();
    if (max == null || cur > max) max = cur;
    maxCount.update(max);

    // reset for next stage
    currentCount.clear();
    lastEventTs.clear();

    // If you need final output after end-of-job, emit elsewhere.
  }
}
```

Notes:
- Register timer at `eventTime + gapMs`. When it fires, you know there was no event in the gap.
- For out-of-order events, assign watermarks (e.g., `forBoundedOutOfOrderness`).

## Pattern B: Session windows
Use when you can compute aggregates with window functions.

```java
stream
  .keyBy(e -> e.jobId)
  .window(EventTimeSessionWindows.withGap(Time.minutes(10)))
  .process(new ProcessWindowFunction<TaskEvent, Tuple2<Long, Integer>, Long, TimeWindow>() {
    @Override
    public void process(Long key, Context ctx, Iterable<TaskEvent> it, Collector<Tuple2<Long, Integer>> out) {
      int count = 0;
      for (TaskEvent e : it) count++;
      out.collect(Tuple2.of(key, count));
    }
  });
```

Then reduce per job to the maximum stage size.

## Common pitfalls
- Convert microsecond timestamps to milliseconds before assigning event time.
- Use SUBMIT events only if the task requires counting submissions.
- Session windows need proper watermarks to close; otherwise windows may not fire.
