# Flink CSV + Gzip Input

## Goal
Read a single `.csv.gz` file in Flink and parse lines into typed objects.

## Setup notes
- Flink can read gzipped text with `readTextFile` or `FileSource.forRecordStreamFormat`.
- For large files, prefer lazy line parsing and avoid splitting more than needed.

## DataStream API (modern)
```java
FileSource<String> source = FileSource.forRecordStreamFormat(
  new TextLineInputFormat(), new Path(inputPath)
).build();

env.fromSource(source, WatermarkStrategy.noWatermarks(), "task-events")
   .map(line -> parse(line));
```

## DataStream API (simple)
```java
env.readTextFile(inputPath) // handles .gz
   .map(line -> parse(line));
```

## Parsing tips
- Use `String.split(",", -1)` to preserve empty columns.
- Guard against malformed lines; consider skipping headers or blank lines.
- Convert timestamps: `eventTimeMs = micros / 1000L`.

## Minimal parser pattern
```java
static TaskEvent parse(String line) {
  String[] f = line.split(",", -1);
  long timeMicros = Long.parseLong(f[0]);
  long jobId = Long.parseLong(f[2]);
  int eventType = Integer.parseInt(f[5]);
  return new TaskEvent(jobId, timeMicros / 1000L, eventType);
}
```
